# leap LineageOS kernel config fragment (merged last, after Motorola's moto-sun-leap.config).
# CONFIG_DRM_DYNAMIC_REFRESH_RATE (drivers/soc/qcom/Kconfig, Motorola-only) has no in-kernel user. D60: it is passed
# to the MODULE builds as a make variable instead (BoardConfigKernelSource.mk), now that our msm_drm exports
# dsi_freq_head; keeping it unset here means the kernel image does not rebuild.
# CONFIG_DRM_DYNAMIC_REFRESH_RATE is not set
# D53: Moto's unified config enables the sibling SoCs; their techpack device trees (kera-camera, kera-gpu, tuna-sde)
# reference bindings the Moto 6.6.82 tree does not ship and fail to parse. leap is sun only.
# CONFIG_ARCH_KERA is not set
# CONFIG_ARCH_TUNA is not set
